{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Vanessa Makes a New Friend", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "What Were You Doing?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 10, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 6, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob10re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " The Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "This is how you form the Past Continuous tense:<br /><br />  subject + was/were + verb-ing<br /> I was cooking.<br /> It was raining.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You often use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense.<br /> The Past Continuous talks about a longer 'background' action. The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class =\"strong\">when</span> and <span class =\"strong\">while</span> before the longer action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "While we were eating, a rainbow appeared over the horizon. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "When we got home, it was raining.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to go on a date", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to spend time with someone who you are romantically interested in ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I went on a date today.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob10aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about what you were doing.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Comparative and Superlative Adjectives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use comparatives to compare people and things with other people and things.<br/> Comparative adjectives are forms like <span class=\"italic\">taller</span>, <span class=\"italic\">more attractive</span>.<br/> You use <span class=\"strong\">than</span> after comparatives .<br/><br/> We use superlatives to compare people and things with all of the group that they are in. <br/> Superlative adjectives are forms like <span class=\"italic\">the tallest</span>, <span class=\"italic\">the most attractive</span>.<br/> You add <span class=\"strong\">the</span> in front of the superlative form to describe people, places and things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " Look at the chart for information on how to form the comparative and superlative:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Adjective</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Comparative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Superlative</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class =\\\"strong\\\">Form</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" tall\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" taller (than) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the tallest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Most adjectives: +-er, +-est\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"late   \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"later (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the latest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Adjectives ending in -e: +-r, +-st\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happy\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"happier (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the happiest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"2-syllable adjectives ending in -y: +-ier, +iest\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"attractive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more attractive (than) \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the most attractive \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"3+-syllable adjectives:  more + adjective + than <br> or<br>the most + adjective\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"good<br /> bad\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"better (than)<br /> worse (than)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"the best<br /> the worst\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Irregular comparisons\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "He's more considerate than other guys. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "It was the most incredible moment!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "rainbow", "type": "name"}, {"content": "different colors in the sky caused by light going through water ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A rainbow appeared in the sky.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob10aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "horizon", "type": "name"}, {"content": "in the distance, where the sky meets the land ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A rainbow appeared on the horizon.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le06ob10aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "considerate", "type": "name"}, {"content": "polite", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He is very considerate.", "type": "example"}, 